.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt TAR 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tar
.Nd create, list and extract native uncompressed ustar archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c | Fl t | Fl x
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl f Ar archive
.Op Fl C Ar directory
.Op Ar member ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This substantial adaptation of sbase 0.1 creates, lists and extracts standard
uncompressed ustar archives containing regular files and directories.
A dash archive name uses standard input or output. Named members select
those paths and their descendants. Creation traverses directories recursively.
Verbose output goes to standard error, not archive bytes.
.Xr sbase 7
records origin and license.
.Sh NATIVE METADATA
Extraction restores contents and hierarchy, not Unix owners, timestamps or
execute/set-ID bits. Regular files become readonly when the archive lacks
owner-write; writable files use native creation semantics. Directories use
native creation without chmod. The -m flag explicitly requests the already
native no-time-restoration behavior; preservation flags are refused.
.Sh LIMITS
Compression, symbolic and hard links, devices, FIFOs, GNU/PAX/sparse extensions,
absolute member names, parent components and unsupported flags are refused.
Source and destination pathname bindings must stay stable during operations;
no concurrent replacement or rollback guarantee is made. Earlier members and
a partial current file may remain after failure. Unsupported or malformed
input and reported I/O errors return nonzero; external termination is separate.
Native ustar bounds and the process resource envelope apply.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr diff 1 ,
.Xr hexdump 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
